Module 4: Anti-aliasing Filter and ADC Input Network

Purpose:
- Limit bandwidth to prevent aliasing; match ADC input requirements and provide bias/CM control.

Schematic description:
- Differential LC or active 4th-order low-pass/bandpass filter between driver outputs and ADC pins.
- Example passive approach: series inductors Ls per leg (10-30 nH) and shunt caps Cs to ground (2-5 pF) tuned for ~100-140 MHz bandpass; simulate in ADS.
- Include series damping resistors Rs (2-10Ω) at ADC inputs for stability.
- Provide Vcm bias (VREF/2) to ADC inputs via large resistors (10k-49.9k) and decouple with 10nF to ground.

Components:
- Precision inductors (surface mount, RF type), high SRF caps, resistors 0402 or 0201 for low parasitics.

Verification:
- Use VNA to verify frequency response; tune L/C values to achieve desired passband and ripple.
